  "id": "monochromatic-light",
  "term": "monochromatic light",
  "definition": "Monochromatic light is light made up of a single wavelength, such as short-wavelength or middle-wavelength light matched to the peak sensitivity of different retinal cone types. In this context, switching between two monochromatic lights changes where the eye focuses and can alter refractive and eye-growth responses.",
